{"name":"Lucky Day","hex":"#929a7d","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lucky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Favoured by luck; fortunate; having good success or good fortune.","Producing, or resulting in, good fortune"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["seven"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lucky Day (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Lucky Day is the sixth studio album released by Jamaican singer Shaggy. It was released on October 29, 2002. The album peaked at number 24 on the Billboard 200 and later reached Gold certification. Three singles were released from the album: \"Hey Sexy Lady\", \"Strength of a Woman\" and \"Get My Party On\". The album featured guest appearances from Shaggy's longtime collaborators Brian and Tony Gold, as well as a guest appearance from Chaka Khan. The song \"We Are the Ones\" was included on the album Barbie Mix, which was released to promote the My Scene dolls."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Day_(album)"},{"title":"Lucky Day (Doctor Who)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lucky Day\" is the fourth episode of the fifteenth series of the British science-fiction television series Doctor Who. It was written by Pete McTighe, and was directed by Peter Hoar. The episode was released on BBC iPlayer, BBC One and Disney+ on 3 May 2025. It features the return of companion Ruby Sunday, who plays a leading role in the episode opposite Conrad Clark, with both the Fifteenth Doctor and Belinda Chandra, the series' main leads, only appearing briefly. The episode focuses on Ruby, who begins a relationship with podcaster Conrad Clark as she attempts to find her place in the world after leaving the Doctor. When Conrad's true aim to turn the public against military organisation UNIT is revealed, Ruby and Kate Lethbridge-Stewart have to deal with the repercussions of Conrad's actions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg/330px-Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucky_Day_(Doctor_Who)"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/94/Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg/250px-Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/94/Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/94/Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg/250px-Lucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALucky_Day_Shaggy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg/330px-Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/36/Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg/330px-Doctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADoctor_Who_Lucky_Day.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Millie_Gibson_2.png/500px-Millie_Gibson_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Millie_Gibson_2.png/500px-Millie_Gibson_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMillie_Gibson_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Jonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJonah_Hauer-King_at_the_2024_Toronto_International_Film_Festival_2_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Jolly_Sailor%2C_Porthcawl_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4975900.jpg/500px-Jolly_Sailor%2C_Porthcawl_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4975900.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Jolly_Sailor%2C_Port